 # Voxelization
 
-Also called: Volume discretization, Grid mapping, Scan-conversion to volume
 
 ## Overview
-Voxelization is the process of mapping a continuous conceptual or physical source (such as a triangle mesh, point cloud, or implicit function) into a discrete volumetric representation suitable for rendering or processing [G]. It solves the problem of converting arbitrary geometric primitives or simulation data into a fixed-size array of grid cells (voxels) that can be efficiently accessed by ray marchers, simulators, or compression algorithms. It differs from [Procedural and implicit volumes](13-procedural-and-implicit-volumes.md) by producing a discrete, stored grid rather than an analytic function, and from [Acquisition](14-acquisition.md) by being a deterministic conversion of known geometry rather than a reconstruction from sensor noise.
