-### [Voxel Occupancy Test](1281-voxel-occupancy-test.md)
-The Voxel Occupancy Test determines whether a given query point lies within an occupied voxel of a pre-computed voxel grid. It solves the problem of spatial containment queries for discrete volumetric data, returning a binary result (occupied or empty) for each input coordinate. Unlike [Analytic Voxelization](10493-analytic-voxelization.md) which computes occupancy on-the-fly via signed distance functions, or [Point Cloud Voxelization](1000-point-cloud-voxelization.md) which generates the grid, this method performs a direct lookup against an existing discrete structure. It differs from [Voxel Visibility Culling](8235-voxel-visibility-culling.md) by testing for general volume inclusion rather than surface-adjacency based on scalar thresholds.
+Generates labeled voxel grids from sequential scan data by managing occlusions and temporal consistency between prior and target states. Chosen for creating discrete volumetric representations from sparse, potentially occluded sensor data.
 
 ### [Virtual Voxel](1987-virtual-voxel.md)
-Virtual Voxel is a rasterization-based voxel renderer designed for the real-time visualization and modification of large-scale voxel scenes (e.g., $4^{12}$ resolution) by combining virtual texture and virtual geometry concepts. It streams appropriate levels of detail into GPU memory using a two-level data structure, storing data linearly to enable efficient real-time editing (Union/Subtraction). Unlike previous graph-based voxel visualization methods, it employs a rasterization rendering pipeline, resulting in highly efficient modification of large scenes.
