-### [Voxelization of Lines and Planes](2472-voxelization-of-lines-and-planes.md)
-This method generates a discrete volumetric representation of 2D lines or 3D planes that is both **N-separating** (topologically robust against N-connected ray penetration) and **N-minimal** (containing no redundant voxels). It solves the problem of topological holes in voxelized surfaces by defining a "slab" of thickness $t$ around the geometric primitive, including only voxels whose centers fall within this slab. Unlike general rasterization-based voxelization [908-rasterization-based-voxelization], this analytic approach guarantees specific connectivity properties (4/8 for 2D, 6/26 for 3D) based on the surface normal and grid resolution, ensuring that 26-connected paths cannot pass through the discretized surface without intersecting a voxel.
