-### Local Voxelization
-Voxelize a mesh in the region of a cube around a specific point, rather than globally. Useful to reduce memory cost for small values of pitch as opposed to global voxelization [S2]. It takes a mesh, a point in space, a pitch (side length of a voxel cube), and a radius (number of voxel cubes to return in each direction) [S2]. When `fill=True`, it uses `proximity.contains` to fill the resulting voxels, which may be meaningless for non-watertight meshes [S2]. Returns a `VoxelGrid` instance with resolution $(m, m, m)$ where $m=2 \times \text{radius} + 1$ [S2].
+### Voxel Matrix Construction via Local Average
+Iterates through each voxel index $i, j, k$ from $0$ to $x\_size-1, y\_size-1, z\_size-1$ respectively [S8, unofficial]. Calculates voxel boundaries: `x_start = i/self.x_size`, `x_end = (i+1)/self.x_size` (similarly for y and z) [S8, unofficial]. Identifies points within the voxel using a boolean mask [S8, unofficial]. If points exist, computes the mean of their RGB values and stores in the voxel matrix [S8, unofficial]. If no points fall within a voxel, returns `[-1.0, -1.0, -1.0]` to indicate an empty voxel [S8, unofficial].
 
